# CFN shared engine registry — single source of truth for worker-engine
# definitions. Consumed by cfn-fleet (templates/engines.env is a symlink to
# this file; run dirs get copies via fleet init) and cfn-tmux-agents
# (lib/engines.sh reads it directly). Edit HERE to change fleet-wide
# defaults; edit a run-dir copy to tune one fleet run.
#
# One engine per line, 7 fields joined by " | " (space pipe space):
#   name | bin | args | set | unset | trust_keys | banner_regex
#   set:         comma list of NAME=$SOURCE_VAR (resolved from the master
#                shell env at spawn time) or NAME=literal
#   unset:       comma list of plain variable names
#   trust_keys:  comma list of keys sent when the folder-trust prompt is seen
#   banner_regex: ERE matched against capture-pane output; unspaced | is
#                regex alternation and allowed
# '#' comments and blank lines are ignored; fields may be empty. A field must
# NOT contain the three-character sequence " | " (that is the separator).
# NO VALUES ON DISK: only variable names and literals that are not secrets.
#
# codex banner carries "Ask Codex": codex-cli 0.153+ renders that instead of
# "provider: openai" (measured 2026-09-10). Spawners must also dismiss the
# codex update modal with "2" (Skip) — never Enter, which picks
# "1. Update now" = surprise npm install -g.
#
# glm unset list carries the data-system credential vars (Airtable / Attio /
# Postgres / Supabase) as a least-privilege DEFAULT: third-party-provider
# panes never hold live data credentials, matching the gg-projects rule
# (write code for those systems, never access them). Projects that
# deliberately want a glm worker to reach a data system remove the name from
# their run-dir copy.
# glm runs through zai-fence.sh (2026-10-10): a macOS sandbox-exec profile that
# confines the worker to its repo root plus Claude Code state, refuses keys,
# Keychain, gh, tmux/docker sockets and in-repo hook/settings writes, and
# fails closed (exit 70). Launchers derive the trust prompt from the first word
# of args when bin is the wrapper. Revert = restore `glm | claude | --model ...`.
claude-sub | claude | --model sonnet --permission-mode bypassPermissions | | ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN,ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_FABLE_MODEL | Down,Enter | Claude Team|Claude Pro|Claude Max
glm | $HOME/.claude/cfn-scripts/zai-fence.sh | claude --model glm-5.3-flash --permission-mode bypassPermissions | ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic,ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=$FLEET_ZAI_TOKEN,CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_UNKNOWN_MODEL_WINDOW_ENFORCEMENT=1 | ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_FABLE_MODEL,AIRTABLE_API_KEY,AIRTABLE_TOKEN,ATTIO_API_KEY,DATABASE_URL,POSTGRES_URL,SUPABASE_URL,SUPABASE_ANON_KEY,SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY | Down,Enter | glm-
# Optional engine (2026-10-10): claude-opus, a subscription worker on Opus for
# plan-critical or hard-debugging workstreams. Off by default because Opus
# burns the subscription budget much faster than Sonnet. To enable it,
# uncomment the line below in the run-dir copy (planning/fleet-*/engines.env),
# then `fleet add WSxx "task" --engine claude-opus`. Same unset list and
# banner as claude-sub.
# claude-opus | claude | --model opus --permission-mode bypassPermissions | | ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN,ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_SONNET_MODEL,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_OPUS_MODEL,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_HAIKU_MODEL,ANTHROPIC_DEFAULT_FABLE_MODEL | Down,Enter | Claude Team|Claude Pro|Claude Max
codex | codex | --sandbox workspace-write --ask-for-approval never | | OPENAI_API_KEY | Enter | provider: openai|OpenAI Codex|Ask Codex
